.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt PAM-CIBA 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pam-ciba
.Nd push-approved PAM sign-in through an OpenID Provider
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -config Ar dir
.Cm authenticate
.Nm
.Op Fl -config Ar dir
.Cm check Ar user
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility signs a local account in through an OpenID Provider's
Client-Initiated Backchannel Authentication flow in poll mode. It is run by
.Xr pam_exec 8
in a PAM auth stack. It asks the provider to have the end-user the local
account maps to approve the sign-in on their own device, waits for the
answer, and exits 0 once the provider issues an ID token that verifies and
names that end-user. It asks the terminal nothing.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width ".Fl -config Ar dir"
.It Fl -config Ar dir
The configuration directory. The default is
.Ev CONFIG_DIR ,
else
.Pa /etc/pam-ciba .
.It Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "authenticate"
.It Cm authenticate
Sign in the account named by
.Ev PAM_USER .
.Ev PAM_RHOST
and
.Ev PAM_SERVICE
fill the binding message. Run by
.Xr pam_exec 8 .
.It Cm check Ar user
Sign in
.Ar user
and print each step.
.El
.Sh PAM CONFIGURATION
Two lines in the service's auth stack:
.Bd -literal
auth [success=ok ignore=ignore default=die] pam_exec.so quiet /usr/bin/pam-ciba authenticate
auth [success=done default=die] pam_permit.so
.Ed
.Pp
The first line runs the sign-in and ends the stack on any failure. The
second line ends the stack on success and answers the credential step,
which
.Xr pam_exec 8
leaves unanswered.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "PAM_SERVICE"
.It Ev CONFIG_DIR
The configuration directory when
.Fl -config
is not given.
.It Ev PAM_USER
The local account to sign in.
.It Ev PAM_RHOST
The remote host of the sign-in.
.It Ev PAM_RUSER
The remote user of the sign-in.
.It Ev PAM_TTY
The terminal of the sign-in.
.It Ev PAM_SERVICE
The PAM service of the sign-in.
.It Ev PAM_TYPE
The PAM stack;
.Cm authenticate
runs only for
.Li auth .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/pam-ciba/app.config.yaml"
.It Pa /etc/pam-ciba/app.config.yaml
The configuration; see
.Xr pam-ciba.yaml 5 .
.It Pa /var/log/pam-ciba/pam-ciba.log
The log.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A sign-in the end-user denies, leaves unanswered until the request expires,
or that the provider refuses exits non-zero.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pam-ciba.yaml 5 ,
.Xr pam_exec 8 ,
.Xr sshd_config 5
.Sh STANDARDS
OpenID Connect Client-Initiated Backchannel Authentication Flow - Core 1.0,
poll mode. OpenID Connect Core 1.0, ID Token Validation.
